TITLE:: RCOrgnsmPatterns
summary:: The pattern library for orgnsms
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCOrgnsm, Classes/RCRhythmDict, Classes/RCPathControl

DESCRIPTION::
All patterns read the orgnsm through the event (code::ev.self::) so they can live in a template and serve every clone. Plazy bodies receive the event under construction: code::Plazy { |ev| ev.self.staticAttrs }:: replaces the old code::~pat.self.dereference.static_attrs::.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: seqParams
Loop after loop of link::#*seqParamsForLoop:: over code::staticAttrs.seq_list::, aligned on the earliest subseq shift. Use in code::addFirstArrayBase:: as code::compute_seq_params: RCOrgnsmPatterns.seqParams(true):: and read code::ev.compute_seq_params.dereference[\dur]:: / code::[key]::.
argument:: returnDict
true: Ref'd Dictionary per value; false: code::[dur, params...]:: arrays.
METHOD:: seqParamsForLoop
One loop of code::seq_list:: merged into one stream. Entries are link::Classes/RCSubseq:: objects (from link::Classes/RCRhythmDict#-subseqs::) or raw code::[priority, shift, durs, params, mask, name, keysIgnoreOrder, timeMult]:: arrays written by hand; a Boolean or missing mask means every hit.
One loop merged from subseqs with an offset-aware scheduler: a hit at the loop start keeps its length and no zero-length rest trails the loop.
argument:: useOrgnsmStaticAttrs
argument:: staticAttrs
argument:: initialBegShift
argument:: returnDict
METHOD:: euclidDurAmp
code::[dur, amp]:: pairs from code::staticAttrs.amp_params:: (code::[[onsets, shift, amp], ...]::) over code::dur_params = [loopDur, pulses]::.
METHOD:: numFramesPerLoop
METHOD:: cuttingFadeStart
Buffer start position: real-time tracking at code::cutting_fade:: 0, Brownian/serial cutting at 1. The cursor lives in the orgnsm's static attributes (per orgnsm) or in strong::holder:: to share it.
argument:: cursorKey
argument:: holder
METHOD:: loop
code::Pn(Plazy(func)):: that cannot spin: a body yielding nothing rests one beat.
